# API & Data Fetching

## HTTP Service Layer

- All API calls go through a dedicated service (e.g., `ApiService`, `UserService`)
- **Never** make direct `HttpClient` calls inside components
- Services are injected into components via `inject()` or constructor

## API Service Pattern

```typescript
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class UserService {
  private http = inject(HttpClient);
  private apiUrl = environment.apiUrl;

  getUsers(): Observable<User[]> {
    return this.http.get<User[]>(`${this.apiUrl}/users`);
  }

  getUser(id: string): Observable<User> {
    return this.http.get<User>(`${this.apiUrl}/users/${id}`);
  }

  createUser(data: CreateUserDto): Observable<User> {
    return this.http.post<User>(`${this.apiUrl}/users`, data);
  }
}
```

## Data Fetching in Components

- [ ] Always handle **loading state**
- [ ] Always handle **error state**
- [ ] Use **signals** for fetched data state
- [ ] Use `async` pipe or `takeUntilDestroyed` to manage subscriptions
- [ ] Never fetch data directly in templates
- [ ] Unsubscribe from Observables to prevent memory leaks (use `takeUntilDestroyed`)

```typescript
export class UserListComponent {
  private userService = inject(UserService);
  private destroyRef = inject(DestroyRef);

  users = signal<User[]>([]);
  loading = signal(false);
  error = signal<string | null>(null);

  ngOnInit() {
    this.loading.set(true);
    this.userService.getUsers()
      .pipe(takeUntilDestroyed(this.destroyRef))
      .subscribe({
        next: (data) => {
          this.users.set(data);
          this.loading.set(false);
        },
        error: (err) => {
          this.error.set('Failed to load users');
          this.loading.set(false);
        },
      });
  }
}
```

## Environment Configuration

- Store API base URLs in `src/environments/environment.ts` and `environment.production.ts`
- Never hardcode API URLs in services or components

## Request Patterns

### Query Parameters

```typescript
getUsers(page: number, pageSize: number): Observable<User[]> {
  const params = new HttpParams()
    .set('page', page.toString())
    .set('pageSize', pageSize.toString());
  return this.http.get<User[]>(`${this.apiUrl}/users`, { params });
}
```

### File Uploads

```typescript
uploadFile(file: File): Observable<UploadResponse> {
  const formData = new FormData();
  formData.append('file', file);
  // Note: Do NOT set Content-Type header — browser sets it with boundary
  return this.http.post<UploadResponse>(`${this.apiUrl}/upload`, formData);
}
```

### Error Handling

```typescript
// Service-level catch + rethrow
getUser(id: string): Observable<User> {
  return this.http.get<User>(`${this.apiUrl}/users/${id}`).pipe(
    catchError((err) => {
      console.error('API error:', err);
      return throw(() => err);
    })
  );
}

// Component-level: show user-friendly message
error: (err) => {
  this.error.set('Không thể tải dữ liệu. Vui lòng thử lại.');
}
```

## RxJS Best Practices

- Use `takeUntilDestroyed` to auto-unsubscribe on component destroy
- Use `switchMap` for cancelable requests (e.g., search-as-you-type)
- Use `shareReplay(1)` for caching shared Observables
- Avoid nested subscriptions — use `switchMap`, `mergeMap`, `forkJoin`
- Use `retry(1)` for transient API failures
